00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.724
SEBASTIEN MAROTTE: Grazie.

00:08:38.724 --> 00:08:41.856
Grazie mille, Nicola,
and buongiorno.

00:08:41.856 --> 00:08:42.480
Now, I'm sorry.

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:46.720
I'm going to switch to
English with a French accent.

00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:50.315
I will be one of the very few
English speakers here today.

00:08:50.315 --> 00:08:50.940
So don't worry.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.500
Actually, we have
really made sure

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.760
that all the local team is
going to run this event.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.190
So my name is Sebastian,
delighted to be back in Milan,

00:08:59.190 --> 00:08:59.970
really delighted.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.490
I'm very impressed by
the audience today.

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.890
I've been six years
already at Google.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.300
And I had the privilege to start
the Google Enterprise business

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:11.010
six years ago, based in London.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.990
So I spent quite some
time here in Italy

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:14.790
during the past few years.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.090
I am delighted to
recognize so many faces.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:21.150
I think that's probably
the largest ever event we

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.890
have been organized in Italy.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:26.640
And I'm really happy,
maybe, to welcome also

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:29.820
a big, new community, which is
the community of developers.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:31.470
We have many
developers in the room.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:33.430
So thank you all
for being there.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.820
Thank you to our customers
also for attending this event

00:09:35.820 --> 00:09:37.500
and sharing best practices.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:40.440
I think this will be a
great opportunity for all

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.070
the business managers also
to hear from our customers

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:45.810
about their journey
and about how they

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.580
are transforming their company.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.400
So my role here is
to spend 10 minutes

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:55.080
to tell you a bit more where
we are at Google Cloud,

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.865
and maybe for the newcomers,
just to understand

00:09:58.865 --> 00:09:59.740
what is Google Cloud.

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:02.670
And if you think
about Google Cloud,

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:04.530
not only is it the
fastest growing business

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:06.970
of one of the fastest
growing businesses at Google.

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:10.830
But what is really interesting
is that Google Cloud is really

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:13.980
the extension of everything
we are doing at Google.

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:16.590
Since we created this
company in 1998--

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:20.220
I was not there, actually--
but the mission of Google

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:23.010
was really to match
the world information

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:26.980
and really to making sure that
it is accessible and useful.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:27.990
So think about it.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:30.360
I mean, we are all sitting
in companies in enterprise,

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.970
small to medium to
very large companies.

00:10:32.970 --> 00:10:34.680
And it's not much different.

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.870
It's really all about the data.

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:39.450
There is not a single company
I'm visiting right now--

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.300
whether it's a hospital,
it's a retailer,

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.120
it's a manufacturing
company, it's a bank,

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.680
it's an insurance company--

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.230
that doesn't care
right now about data.

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:51.270
I mean, this is what
we are living with.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:55.620
This is our main asset to
really manage our business.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:58.800
So this is what we are
providing to the world.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:02.700
In addition to being able to
manage this very large amount

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:09.390
of data, we are providing the
best scalable, open and secure

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.676
architecture to
make it possible.

00:11:11.676 --> 00:11:13.800
We have made a lot of
investments in the last three

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:14.440
years.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:16.980
I mean, it is becoming
extremely mainstream.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.520
If you were-- for those who
visited us three years ago,

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:22.580
we were a 3,000, 4,000
people organization.

00:11:22.580 --> 00:11:25.450
Now we are close to a
14,000 people organization.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.672
So we have spent
close to $30 billion

00:11:28.672 --> 00:11:32.160
on our infrastructure
in our CAPEX.

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:36.660
So we all know that there is
a momentum around the cloud,

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:37.330
actually.

00:11:37.330 --> 00:11:39.990
And let me be a little
bit candid here.

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:42.750
I think that we
are just starting

00:11:42.750 --> 00:11:46.110
to begin understanding
the shape of the future.

00:11:46.110 --> 00:11:49.210
Things are just starting
to really start,

00:11:49.210 --> 00:11:50.857
if I may say it
like that, actually.

00:11:50.857 --> 00:11:52.440
Compared to a few
years ago, everybody

00:11:52.440 --> 00:11:54.250
was welcoming this
kind of event.

00:11:54.250 --> 00:11:56.489
And everybody was
talking about the cloud,

00:11:56.489 --> 00:11:57.780
about the benefit of the cloud.

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.680
You can cut the bill.

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.138
You can transform
the way you work.

00:12:00.138 --> 00:12:01.500
You can connect people.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.480
You can surface new ideas.

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:06.150
Yeah, true, actually, that
was very, very marketing-

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:07.600
and sales-driven.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:11.400
But I really believe that things
are coming together right now.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.310
And I think we are really
entering in a new world

00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:18.210
where you have the opportunity
to share all these resources

00:12:18.210 --> 00:12:20.520
and services that
are now totally

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:24.360
accessible from absolutely
anywhere, any kind of device.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:25.350
Remember that.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.660
It is five years we
are talking about--

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.520
anywhere, any kind of devices.

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:32.030
But today, it is
really improving.

00:12:32.030 --> 00:12:35.340
And all these services
are available to you

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:38.760
as an individual or as
a team or as a company.

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.807
But these services are improving
all the time, actually.

00:12:41.807 --> 00:12:43.140
You're waking up in the morning.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.770
You're switching your mobile.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:45.420
And off you go.

00:12:45.420 --> 00:12:46.440
You have new services.

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:47.190
You have new data.

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:49.890
You have new insightful data.

00:12:49.890 --> 00:12:53.096
And you have real-time
analysis capabilities

00:12:53.096 --> 00:12:53.970
that you didn't have.

00:12:53.970 --> 00:13:00.210
So the power of the cloud is
really available for everyone.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:02.730
And so not only it is
available, but it's really

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:07.200
empowering as individual
employees and to meet

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.580
our professional goals.

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:12.000
And I think if we manage
all of this correctly,

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.800
I really believe that
we can dramatically

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:17.520
improve the way we are
performing and the way we live.

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.730
So it doesn't work without
the right infrastructure.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.860
And a lot of times,
actually, when

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:26.310
I'm visiting some
customers and partners,

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.680
we are being asked,
what makes Google

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:31.420
different from the
rest of the industry?

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:33.750
And I think, at the end
of the day, what makes

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.610
a real difference is our DNA.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:37.140
It's all the
investment we have done

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.520
to build this Google network
that you're seeing here

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.640
on the screen.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.550
We have an undisputed--

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.340
we have a very
advanced infrastructure

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:49.140
with the network we
have been building

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.770
with our assets and
the many data centers,

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:53.860
actually, that we have
been building in the world.

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:55.890
Think about the number
of points of presence

00:13:55.890 --> 00:13:57.420
we are having in the world.

00:13:57.420 --> 00:14:00.420
You can access this network
from pretty much everywhere

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:01.500
in the world.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:05.370
That gives you, by far,
the fastest performance

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:07.950
to run your data.

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.810
And this is really ongoing.

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:13.470
We're heavily investing
in opening new regions.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:16.950
We are opening new
data centers in London,

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:20.610
in Amsterdam, in Frankfurt
in the next coming few weeks.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:23.490
And all of these regions
are all connected

00:14:23.490 --> 00:14:27.450
with super high-speed fast
cable that we have rolled out

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.960
across the world.

00:14:28.960 --> 00:14:34.260
So our capacity to stream
data is almost unlimited.

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:35.880
And it's just
absolutely amazing.

00:14:35.880 --> 00:14:37.890
If you think about
it, a few years ago,

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:41.340
like just 15 years
ago, it took ages just

00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:46.150
to upload a single picture
which was the size of the stamp.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:51.870
Now every day, we are streaming
a billion hours of YouTube

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:54.180
content in this network.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:54.977
And this is ours.

00:14:54.977 --> 00:14:57.060
But this is also yours,
because we are opening it.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:14:59.700
So it's not only about
an infrastructure.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.580
As Nicola said, we
are providing services

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.410
on top of this infrastructure.

00:15:04.410 --> 00:15:07.680
And you know that these
services are ready,

00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:13.680
available 24 by 7 to you.

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:15.510
Sorry, they are
available, actually,

00:15:15.510 --> 00:15:17.820
for your personal usage.

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:19.680
And these services,
we are spending

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:22.290
a lot of time, effort,
and investment also

00:15:22.290 --> 00:15:25.310
to making sure that they
are absolutely secure.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:28.420
And also, we care about
privacy and trust.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:30.660
So we have seven
products or services

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:34.620
that are being used by more
than a billion users every day.

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:37.830
And for our Google Cloud
Platform customers,

00:15:37.830 --> 00:15:42.060
they are even servicing a
billion users on their own

00:15:42.060 --> 00:15:43.630
every day.

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:46.944
So this is the services
and the platform.

00:15:46.944 --> 00:15:49.110
If you think about some
products like Google Search,

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.250
for instance, you
wouldn't believe it,

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:54.960
but we have more than 2
trillion search queries that

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:57.480
are being run on a single year.

00:15:57.480 --> 00:15:59.630
So it requires an
enormous infrastructure.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:02.930
And when I was thinking and
talking about different shares,

00:16:02.930 --> 00:16:05.430
I mean, being successful
in the cloud is really

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:06.960
about a few pillars.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:10.320
And infrastructure and
network is absolutely

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:14.009
on the very, very
top of the pile.

00:16:14.009 --> 00:16:16.050
You may hear about all of
these stories regarding

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:18.510
data and machine
learning and analytics.

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:20.400
You are not going
to run properly

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:22.720
your data and your
analytics if you're not

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:25.260
at the right
infrastructure that is

00:16:25.260 --> 00:16:27.690
being able and
available for absolutely

00:16:27.690 --> 00:16:29.530
everyone across the world.

00:16:29.530 --> 00:16:31.200
So we have, of
course, many customers

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:34.440
that have built their business
on this infrastructure.

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.422
I mean, whether you
are a startup company,

00:16:36.422 --> 00:16:38.130
the last thing you
want to do is to build

00:16:38.130 --> 00:16:39.210
your own infrastructure.

00:16:39.210 --> 00:16:41.460
Or you're a [INAUDIBLE]
enterprise company,

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.130
you're going to use
this infrastructure.

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:46.020
So this is the example of
this company called Niantic.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:50.610
We all know about this amazing
game, which was "Pokemon Go."

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:53.700
And never, ever
"Pokemon Go" would have

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:56.400
existed without Google Cloud.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:16:58.320
I mean, this is
the main feedback

00:16:58.320 --> 00:17:00.690
that we received from the
team and from the CEO.

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:04.319
The main reason being that when
they launched "Pokemon Go,"

00:17:04.319 --> 00:17:08.730
they have exceeded the
predicted demand by 50.

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:09.839
Think about it, actually.

00:17:09.839 --> 00:17:12.569
You're launching a new service,
a new business, a new product.

00:17:12.569 --> 00:17:17.880
And suddenly, day one, you're
multiplying by 50 any best case

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.470
expectation.

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.720
And if you think
about it, if you

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:24.930
had to launch this
product or these services

00:17:24.930 --> 00:17:30.240
on premise and with provisioning
all the infrastructure

00:17:30.240 --> 00:17:33.360
on premise, I mean, it would
just have not been possible

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.280
in terms of cost and logistics.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:37.110
So this is what they have done.

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:40.490
And we are absolutely
ready to take massive loads

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:43.410
and to really manage an
expected peak period.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:47.310
So it's really an
exciting story.

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:50.910
And what is also exciting is
that "Pokemon Go" is probably

00:17:50.910 --> 00:17:54.540
the best story we have when
it comes to content management

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:59.130
and the largest ever Kubernetes
deployment we have done.

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:03.060
And they are using more than
12 services across Google.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.579
The other one is Snap.

00:18:04.579 --> 00:18:06.370
If you think about this
company's Snapchat,

00:18:06.370 --> 00:18:08.970
they came to us
in November 2011.

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:12.350
And they had a very
simple inquiry.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:13.780
We want to launch new services.

00:18:13.780 --> 00:18:16.405
But the last thing we want to do
is to build an infrastructure.

00:18:16.405 --> 00:18:20.280
We really want to focus on
developing our own application.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:23.250
And it's fascinating to see what
we have done with these guys,

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:24.480
actually with Snap.

00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:28.170
It's absolutely fascinating that
you can write a bit of code--

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:32.610
well, a bit, quite
some amount of code--

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:35.940
drop it in a container,
and everything

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:37.910
is being taken care of.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.830
I mean, whether
it's about scaling,

00:18:39.830 --> 00:18:44.420
it's about availability,
it's about security,

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:46.280
you don't really
need to know how

00:18:46.280 --> 00:18:48.270
to manage and to run systems.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:49.820
So by contrast, if
you think-- and we

00:18:49.820 --> 00:18:53.420
are seeing a lot of startup
companies in the market

00:18:53.420 --> 00:18:55.170
that didn't go
that pass and that

00:18:55.170 --> 00:19:00.710
are failing because they are
facing a lot of outages issues

00:19:00.710 --> 00:19:04.870
by using their own premise
and their own infrastructure.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.510
So at Google Cloud, we care
about all these services.

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:10.900
But at Google Cloud, we also
launch a lot of new services.

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:13.900
And I think that this morning,
if you have the opportunity,

00:19:13.900 --> 00:19:16.360
spend some time
trying to understand

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:19.840
what is this Cloud Spanner
scalable transactions

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:20.980
processing system?

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.480
It's absolutely amazing.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:24.070
You won't find any
kind of services

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:25.820
like that across the world.

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:29.020
You can also access our
real-time or near real-time

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:33.100
data warehousing BigQuery and
data analytics with BigQuery.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.470
And we have spent a lot of time.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:38.100
And every day, we are
releasing some new features

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:40.120
around our machine
learning engines

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:41.980
and around our smart APIs.

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:46.300
It's amazing to see what you
can really build as new use case

00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:51.370
when it comes to Video API to
Vision API, natural language

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:52.600
recognition.

00:19:52.600 --> 00:19:55.185
We are even working on
Job APIs to making sure

00:19:55.185 --> 00:19:56.560
that we can really
better connect

00:19:56.560 --> 00:20:00.546
your enterprise with
employees in the marketplace.

00:20:00.546 --> 00:20:02.920
And we are really seeing all
of this based on these cloud

00:20:02.920 --> 00:20:05.200
machine learning engines.

00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:10.120
So when you think about
big data and analytics,

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:12.730
there is a very interesting case
that we have been working on.

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.620
And we've made a
public announcement

00:20:14.620 --> 00:20:16.770
two months ago in San
Francisco with Darryl

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.300
West, the global CIO.

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:22.450
HSBC, which is probably one
of the largest and the oldest

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:26.040
bank in the world, they've
been created 150 years ago,

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.300
I decided, actually,
to go to the cloud

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:33.580
and to start with a Google for
all their analytical platform.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.740
Again, go to YouTube
and you will see Darryl.

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:39.850
But what is very interesting
is that a company like HSBC,

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:44.410
it took them 130 years to start
measuring their data volume

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.870
into terabytes, just amazing.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:50.410
Just the last two years,
they got 15 terabytes.

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:53.500
And just this year, they have
to manage an additional 5

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.400
terabytes.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.770
It is really the world
of data explosion.

00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:58.720
And they did a
traditional journey.

00:20:58.720 --> 00:21:00.580
We have large
companies that have

00:21:00.580 --> 00:21:03.330
spent a lot of time, energy, and
money in the traditional data

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.060
warehousing.

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.460
They will recognize this.

00:21:05.460 --> 00:21:08.890
They started a long time ago
with a traditional relational

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:09.490
database.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.970
And then they moved, because
of the volume of data,

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.470
to the data
warehousing structure.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:15.790
It was great, actually.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:16.390
It was great.

00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:19.120
When you sent to HSBC
[INAUDIBLE] data warehousing

00:21:19.120 --> 00:21:20.350
[INAUDIBLE] was great.

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:23.170
But it became, very quickly,
extremely complex to maintain

00:21:23.170 --> 00:21:24.830
and extremely expensive.

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:28.750
So they moved to the big
data era with Hadoop.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:31.607
And honestly, it's saying, we
have faced a lot of challenges.

00:21:31.607 --> 00:21:33.190
I mean, this was
probably the only way

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:35.690
to manage a large,
large load of data.

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:39.190
But again, it was
extremely expensive.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.020
And so it was extremely
tough, actually,

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:42.790
because they had to
feed this new system.

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.610
They had to train
their employees.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:49.750
And very quickly, it became
very expensive and quite

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:50.727
difficult to maintain.

00:21:50.727 --> 00:21:51.310
So they moved.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:53.800
They have decided to move to
Google Cloud Platform, which

00:21:53.800 --> 00:21:56.381
was much easier
and much cheaper.

00:21:56.381 --> 00:21:57.880
If you think about
machine learning,

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.340
we have many, many cases
in machine learning.

00:22:00.340 --> 00:22:01.320
And it's amazing.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:03.060
Every day, we are
meeting customers

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:05.050
that are coming with new ideas.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:08.240
This is an idea that
Airbus came to us.

00:22:08.240 --> 00:22:13.780
And one part of this business
is around satellite images.

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:17.500
So they are managing a huge
amount of satellite image.

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.600
So you know it's very
useful for agriculture,

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:20.740
for civil engineering.

00:22:20.740 --> 00:22:23.110
So they really need to
build their business

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:26.590
and to grow their business
on this satellite image.

00:22:26.590 --> 00:22:28.100
But the problem
with satellite image

00:22:28.100 --> 00:22:32.650
is when you picture the
world, you have some defaults.

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:34.150
You don't know how
to differentiate,

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:36.340
for instance, cloud
and snow, just

00:22:36.340 --> 00:22:38.657
if you picture the mountain.

00:22:38.657 --> 00:22:39.990
So you have to clear the clouds.

00:22:39.990 --> 00:22:41.239
You have to separate the snow.

00:22:41.239 --> 00:22:42.850
You have to do a
lot of cleaning.

00:22:42.850 --> 00:22:45.840
And that was a manual
process that Airbus

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:48.700
was running with just
individual people that

00:22:48.700 --> 00:22:51.285
were working weeks, actually,
before coming to these results.

00:22:51.285 --> 00:22:53.910
And thanks to machine
learning, automatically,

00:22:53.910 --> 00:22:56.500
we were able to analyze
all of this information

00:22:56.500 --> 00:23:00.250
and to dramatically shorten
the process to a few hours.

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:04.030
But more importantly, also
to drop the error rates

00:23:04.030 --> 00:23:07.480
from anywhere
close to 15% to 3%.

00:23:07.480 --> 00:23:09.200
So that is another example.

00:23:09.200 --> 00:23:11.170
And we have so many
examples around that,

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:13.592
whether it's in digital
natives or enterprise space.

00:23:13.592 --> 00:23:15.550
I'd like to finish on
two or three things which

00:23:15.550 --> 00:23:16.700
are very close to our hearts.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:18.450
And I know we have a
lot of customers here

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:20.110
who are using G Suite in Italy.

00:23:20.110 --> 00:23:24.320
This is super, super
strategic to our business.

00:23:24.320 --> 00:23:26.050
We really want to help
you, as employees,

00:23:26.050 --> 00:23:27.174
to change the way you work.

00:23:27.174 --> 00:23:28.802
We want to help you
be more productive.

00:23:28.802 --> 00:23:30.760
But being more productive
is about saving time.

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.400
Saving time is about taking
care of you, actually.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:35.890
And we really believe
that we can dramatically

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.890
help you to improve not
only your productivity

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:41.290
in the office, but
your life at home.

00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:43.912
And if you think about some
very large customers like PWC,

00:23:43.912 --> 00:23:45.370
for instance, which
is probably one

00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:48.624
of the most conservative
companies in the world,

00:23:48.624 --> 00:23:49.790
they have made some studies.

00:23:49.790 --> 00:23:52.330
They started the deployment
of Google Suite, G Suite.

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:54.910
And they realized that every
single employee, average,

00:23:54.910 --> 00:24:00.940
was gaining nine hours
a week in the office.

00:24:00.940 --> 00:24:02.330
So it's amazing.

00:24:02.330 --> 00:24:04.670
It's just an amazing
collaborative platform.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:08.600
You can work together without
necessarily being together.

00:24:08.600 --> 00:24:10.520
And it's really a life changer.

00:24:10.520 --> 00:24:12.204
This is absolutely fascinating.

00:24:12.204 --> 00:24:14.120
And the last thing that
Nicola also mentioned,

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:18.590
and we have many,
many customers here,

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:22.830
it's providing the next
generation of devices.

00:24:22.830 --> 00:24:26.120
So you may think about very
conservative and highly

00:24:26.120 --> 00:24:28.026
regulated companies
like Charles Schwab.

00:24:28.026 --> 00:24:29.900
This is the financial
institution, of course,

00:24:29.900 --> 00:24:30.860
in the US.

00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:32.936
They have decided to
roll out Chromebooks,

00:24:32.936 --> 00:24:34.310
because they just
think that this

00:24:34.310 --> 00:24:39.380
is, by far, the most scalable
and secure devices that they

00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:41.030
can use in their organization.

00:24:41.030 --> 00:24:43.430
And there are some
studies which states

00:24:43.430 --> 00:24:45.530
that by 2018, which
is around the corner,

00:24:45.530 --> 00:24:49.190
next year, 25% of the
Fortune 500 companies

00:24:49.190 --> 00:24:51.710
will be using some Chromebooks.

00:24:51.710 --> 00:24:54.650
All right, I wouldn't be
complete without telling you--

00:24:54.650 --> 00:24:57.140
and this is a very
serious topic--

00:24:57.140 --> 00:24:59.450
that we are heavily
investing in security.

00:24:59.450 --> 00:25:02.010
And the next speaker will
tell you more about that.

00:25:02.010 --> 00:25:04.460
But we have taken a very
strong and firm commitment

00:25:04.460 --> 00:25:08.420
that we will be ready
on the GDPR compliance

00:25:08.420 --> 00:25:10.790
by the due date,
which is May 2018.

00:25:10.790 --> 00:25:13.010
And we can also start
working with you,

00:25:13.010 --> 00:25:15.320
with your privacy and
security team, TRUST team,

00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:18.420
actually, on this specific
topic, which is very important.

00:25:18.420 --> 00:25:20.682
So I can talk about
security for ages.

00:25:20.682 --> 00:25:21.890
But we have special sessions.

00:25:21.890 --> 00:25:26.540
So we have more than 800
engineers working on security.

00:25:26.540 --> 00:25:29.160
And it's absolutely central
to everything we are doing.

00:25:29.160 --> 00:25:31.160
If you think about it,
again, the recent events,

00:25:31.160 --> 00:25:33.500
and no later than
yesterday, I think

00:25:33.500 --> 00:25:37.410
cloud can bring you a
lot to defend your data

00:25:37.410 --> 00:25:41.810
and to secure your data,
which is super important.

00:25:41.810 --> 00:25:44.660
Last few things,
partners, Nicola

00:25:44.660 --> 00:25:46.160
mentioned some partnerships.

00:25:46.160 --> 00:25:47.750
We care about the
enterprise space.

00:25:47.750 --> 00:25:50.180
We invest a lot in
the enterprise space.

00:25:50.180 --> 00:25:53.360
And we also have recently
announced some very strategic

00:25:53.360 --> 00:25:58.640
partnerships with companies
like ACP, or Intel.

00:25:58.640 --> 00:25:59.870
This is extremely strategic.

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:00.536
We are studying.

00:26:00.536 --> 00:26:03.950
We are co-developing some
applications with these guys.

00:26:03.950 --> 00:26:06.870
And it's very strategic, too,
for the enterprise space.

00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:09.450
Two things, also, which
are very important.

00:26:09.450 --> 00:26:11.270
Number one, at the
end of the day,

00:26:11.270 --> 00:26:14.580
companies are coming to Google
with a lot of questions.

00:26:14.580 --> 00:26:16.320
This is a very new environment.

00:26:16.320 --> 00:26:18.630
This is a very new ecosystem.

00:26:18.630 --> 00:26:20.980
And honestly, we have a lot
of questions, which is--

00:26:20.980 --> 00:26:21.710
this is great.

00:26:21.710 --> 00:26:24.290
I mean, everything you're
seeing is pretty cool,

00:26:24.290 --> 00:26:26.870
but a lot of
questions regarding,

00:26:26.870 --> 00:26:29.570
how do I start this
kind of project?

00:26:29.570 --> 00:26:33.420
What do I need to build this
next generation application?

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:34.700
Who should I recruit?

00:26:34.700 --> 00:26:37.320
How do I train my people?

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:40.610
A lot of questions regarding,
do I need to rewrite my code?

00:26:40.610 --> 00:26:45.380
Or am I going to be locked
again with a single provider?

00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:48.230
So we have so many questions
that we are not only

00:26:48.230 --> 00:26:49.430
providing a technology.

00:26:49.430 --> 00:26:51.560
But we need to be really
a business trusted advisor

00:26:51.560 --> 00:26:52.500
to your organization.

00:26:52.500 --> 00:26:54.830
So we have built a very
large organization.

00:26:54.830 --> 00:26:58.640
We are doubling our headcount
here in Italy, in Europe,

00:26:58.640 --> 00:26:59.859
and across the world.

00:26:59.859 --> 00:27:01.400
And more importantly,
we are bringing

00:27:01.400 --> 00:27:03.530
more technical
resources in the field.

00:27:03.530 --> 00:27:05.930
So you will see
here, later today,

00:27:05.930 --> 00:27:08.780
customer engineers that will
help you actually to prototype

00:27:08.780 --> 00:27:09.760
your next application.

00:27:09.760 --> 00:27:11.300
You will see a
software architect

00:27:11.300 --> 00:27:14.300
that will help you to
design the next application.

00:27:14.300 --> 00:27:16.820
You will see we have a
dedicated Office of the CTO.

00:27:16.820 --> 00:27:19.970
They're really act
as shared CTOs.

00:27:19.970 --> 00:27:21.924
And they can really advise you.

00:27:21.924 --> 00:27:23.840
And more importantly,
again, for the community

00:27:23.840 --> 00:27:25.850
of developers which
is in Rome, we

00:27:25.850 --> 00:27:29.480
are connecting our engineers
to our customers, which

00:27:29.480 --> 00:27:31.580
is very, very new
compared to everything

00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:32.720
we have done in the past.

00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:36.360
We are widely opening the
doors of our engineers.

00:27:36.360 --> 00:27:38.120
So I will finish
on the one slide,

00:27:38.120 --> 00:27:41.650
which is we are also
being asked, eventually,

00:27:41.650 --> 00:27:43.180
what is the future?

00:27:43.180 --> 00:27:45.040
Things are going so fast.

00:27:45.040 --> 00:27:47.980
And again, candidly, I have
been at Google for six years.

00:27:47.980 --> 00:27:50.740
It is just amazing to see the
pace that we have been through

00:27:50.740 --> 00:27:52.930
during the past 24 months.

00:27:52.930 --> 00:27:57.880
And we really believe that
we are entering in a world

00:27:57.880 --> 00:27:59.590
where you need an idea.

00:27:59.590 --> 00:28:03.070
And you need to be able
to digitalize this idea.

00:28:03.070 --> 00:28:06.520
It's amazing to see how
much, with a great idea,

00:28:06.520 --> 00:28:10.250
how you can turn that
into an amazing project.

00:28:10.250 --> 00:28:13.040
So with the machine
learning, with the smart APIs

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:16.250
I was talking about,
with the highly available

00:28:16.250 --> 00:28:19.810
containerization, its so
easy to build and deploy

00:28:19.810 --> 00:28:22.450
these applications
that can run, really,

00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:25.322
across all the world
on any kind of devices,

00:28:25.322 --> 00:28:27.280
and not only on the
devices we are using today,

00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:29.300
like a laptop, like
a mobile phone,

00:28:29.300 --> 00:28:32.750
but also on sensors, just on the
cloud, and the next generation

00:28:32.750 --> 00:28:35.590
devices that we are
building and that

00:28:35.590 --> 00:28:37.460
are going to get connected.

00:28:37.460 --> 00:28:39.830
So I think that this
data will be shared.

00:28:39.830 --> 00:28:42.680
This data will be
updated, real-time.

00:28:42.680 --> 00:28:45.340
And this data will
be super insightful.

00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:47.290
So I really believe--
we believe that we will

00:28:47.290 --> 00:28:49.090
work all we have to, actually.

00:28:49.090 --> 00:28:52.720
This is for the sake of working
in the most matter, of course,

00:28:52.720 --> 00:28:53.560
and a better world.

00:28:53.560 --> 00:28:56.950
So whether you're in medicine,
in medical, in fintec,

00:28:56.950 --> 00:28:59.730
in manufacturing, in
retail, you build energy.

00:28:59.730 --> 00:29:00.610
You make energy.

00:29:00.610 --> 00:29:02.470
Or you run a media company.

00:29:02.470 --> 00:29:04.990
I think this is going
to really transform

00:29:04.990 --> 00:29:06.780
the way the organizations
are working.

00:29:06.780 --> 00:29:08.740
So we are going
to start answering

00:29:08.740 --> 00:29:11.920
to problems that never, ever
we have been able to resolve.

00:29:11.920 --> 00:29:15.610
I mean, just think about
the medical environment.

00:29:15.610 --> 00:29:19.330
So the cloud, to us, is--

00:29:19.330 --> 00:29:22.720
the best cloud is the cloud
with the best technology.

00:29:22.720 --> 00:29:27.190
Google is really serious
about this business.

00:29:27.190 --> 00:29:29.390
It is really mainstream
to our business.

00:29:29.390 --> 00:29:31.490
We are investing a ton of money.

00:29:31.490 --> 00:29:35.500
And this is what we're going
to share with you this morning.

00:29:35.500 --> 00:29:37.120
We are a company
born in the cloud.

00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:40.570
And we really want to extend the
services to your organization.

00:29:40.570 --> 00:29:41.950
We thank you very much.

00:29:41.950 --> 00:29:44.132
And I will pass it
over to Gabriele, who's

00:29:44.132 --> 00:29:45.340
